  "id": "dmri",
  "term": "dMRI",
  "definition": "dMRI is an MRI-based imaging method that collects images at different b-values, usually with fewer low b-value images and more high b-value images. These measurements are used for later fiber tract tracing and structural analysis, and differences in acquisition methods can affect data quality.",
